    "Start with the order stage, not the map": "Start with the order stage, not the map",
    "Tracking makes sense only after you identify the current order stage. Payment accepted, processing, label created, carrier accepted, export movement, destination processing, out for delivery and delivered are different events. Hacoo's published page says processing normally takes three to five business days and that receiving time combines processing and shipping. An order still being prepared should not be judged by the movement expected after carrier acceptance.": "Tracking makes sense only after you identify the current order stage. Payment accepted, processing, label created, carrier accepted, export movement, destination processing, out for delivery and delivered are different events. Hacoo's published page says processing normally takes three to five business days and that receiving time combines processing and shipping. An order still being prepared should not be judged by the movement expected after carrier acceptance.",
    "Create a timeline from the order screen before opening a third-party tracker. Write down the purchase time, the estimated dispatch or receiving information shown for the order, the moment a tracking number appears and the first event that confirms physical possession by a carrier. This small step prevents the most common confusion: treating an electronic label as if the package had already begun travelling.": "Create a timeline from the order screen before opening a third-party tracker. Write down the purchase time, the estimated dispatch or receiving information shown for the order, the moment a tracking number appears and the first event that confirms physical possession by a carrier. This small step prevents the most common confusion: treating an electronic label as if the package had already begun travelling.",
    "Interpret label-created messages narrowly": "Interpret label-created messages narrowly",
    "A label-created, shipment-information-received or pre-advice message usually means data has been sent to a logistics system. It does not necessarily mean the parcel has reached a facility. The next meaningful event is a collection, acceptance or processing scan. If the record remains at pre-advice, ask whether the order is still within its preparation window before assuming it is lost.": "A label-created, shipment-information-received or pre-advice message usually means data has been sent to a logistics system. It does not necessarily mean the parcel has reached a facility. The next meaningful event is a collection, acceptance or processing scan. If the record remains at pre-advice, ask whether the order is still within its preparation window before assuming it is lost.",
    "Do not repeatedly refresh several aggregators and count their copied entries as separate evidence. Many services display the same underlying event with different wording or time zones. Keep one primary carrier record and use an aggregator only to discover a handoff number. When contacting support, quote the exact event and timestamp rather than saying that tracking â€œdoesn't work.â€ Specific language is easier to investigate.": "Do not repeatedly refresh several aggregators and count their copied entries as separate evidence. Many services display the same underlying event with different wording or time zones. Keep one primary carrier record and use an aggregator only to discover a handoff number. When contacting support, quote the exact event and timestamp rather than saying that tracking â€œdoesn't work.â€ Specific language is easier to investigate.",
    "Recognise export and line-haul events": "Recognise export and line-haul events",
    "Statuses such as departed facility, handed to airline, line-haul departure, export clearance or in transit can describe movement between networks rather than a direct trip to your address. The location shown may be a consolidation hub. Several days without a public scan can occur while a sealed shipment moves or waits for the next network event. Silence alone does not reveal the parcel's condition.": "Statuses such as departed facility, handed to airline, line-haul departure, export clearance or in transit can describe movement between networks rather than a direct trip to your address. The location shown may be a consolidation hub. Several days without a public scan can occur while a sealed shipment moves or waits for the next network event. Silence alone does not reveal the parcel's condition.",
    "Compare the last confirmed event with the estimate attached to the order. If the parcel remains within the broad range, keep monitoring at a sensible interval. If it exceeds the current estimate or a carrier displays an exception, prepare a timeline and use official support. Avoid assigning a cause such as customs seizure, lost flight or seller delay unless the carrier or platform actually states it.": "Compare the last confirmed event with the estimate attached to the order. If the parcel remains within the broad range, keep monitoring at a sensible interval. If it exceeds the current estimate or a carrier displays an exception, prepare a timeline and use official support. Avoid assigning a cause such as customs seizure, lost flight or seller delay unless the carrier or platform actually states it.",
    "Follow carrier handoffs explicitly": "Follow carrier handoffs explicitly",
    "International tracking often changes when a destination carrier receives the parcel. The original page may say handed over, arrived at destination or transferred to local delivery partner. Look for a new tracking identifier, carrier name or link. Enter that number on the destination carrier's official website and compare the first local event with the final event in the origin network.": "International tracking often changes when a destination carrier receives the parcel. The original page may say handed over, arrived at destination or transferred to local delivery partner. Look for a new tracking identifier, carrier name or link. Enter that number on the destination carrier's official website and compare the first local event with the final event in the origin network.",
    "Store both numbers together because support may reference either one. A handoff can produce duplicate or apparently reversed timestamps when systems use different time zones. Sort the events by the displayed local time only after noting each zone, and focus on sequence: export network completion, destination acceptance, local sorting and delivery attempt. The goal is a usable record, not a perfectly animated map.": "Store both numbers together because support may reference either one. A handoff can produce duplicate or apparently reversed timestamps when systems use different time zones. Sort the events by the displayed local time only after noting each zone, and focus on sequence: export network completion, destination acceptance, local sorting and delivery attempt. The goal is a usable record, not a perfectly animated map.",
    "Treat exceptions as instructions": "Treat exceptions as instructions",
    "Address problem, delivery attempted, held for collection, customs information required and returned to sender are not ordinary transit updates. They normally require a check or action. Open the official carrier record, verify that the message belongs to your tracking number and use the contact route published by that carrier. Never pay a surprise charge through a link in an unsolicited text without independently verifying the domain and parcel.": "Address problem, delivery attempted, held for collection, customs information required and returned to sender are not ordinary transit updates. They normally require a check or action. Open the official carrier record, verify that the message belongs to your tracking number and use the contact route published by that carrier. Never pay a surprise charge through a link in an unsolicited text without independently verifying the domain and parcel.",
    "For an address issue, Hacoo's policy tells buyers to contact Hacoo immediately because the correction window can be small. Once the parcel is with a carrier, rerouting may depend on carrier rules and local practice. Save any case or reference number. If the carrier says only the sender can act, pass that response to the platform rather than opening disconnected conversations across multiple channels.": "For an address issue, Hacoo's policy tells buyers to contact Hacoo immediately because the correction window can be small. Once the parcel is with a carrier, rerouting may depend on carrier rules and local practice. Save any case or reference number. If the carrier says only the sender can act, pass that response to the platform rather than opening disconnected conversations across multiple channels.",
    "Handle a delivered scan methodically": "Handle a delivered scan methodically",
    "Hacoo's published page says that when tracking marks a parcel delivered but it has not been received, the buyer should report the issue to the relevant carrier; it also points to customer support for further questions. Begin with the recorded delivery time, location, photograph or signature if available. Check household members, reception, parcel lockers and the safe-place area shown by the carrier.": "Hacoo's published page says that when tracking marks a parcel delivered but it has not been received, the buyer should report the issue to the relevant carrier; it also points to customer support for further questions. Begin with the recorded delivery time, location, photograph or signature if available. Check household members, reception, parcel lockers and the safe-place area shown by the carrier.",
    "Open a carrier investigation through the official route and save its reference. Then update the platform case with the exact tracking record and carrier response. Do not publish your address, phone number or tracking number on a forum. A delivered scan is evidence that the carrier recorded a delivery, not automatic proof that the parcel reached the intended recipient or that a refund is due.": "Open a carrier investigation through the official route and save its reference. Then update the platform case with the exact tracking record and carrier response. Do not publish your address, phone number or tracking number on a forum. A delivered scan is evidence that the carrier recorded a delivery, not automatic proof that the parcel reached the intended recipient or that a refund is due.",
    "Document split shipments separately": "Document split shipments separately",
    "The official shipping page says available items may ship before pre-ordered or back-ordered products. If an order creates two parcels, each needs its own timeline. Match items to tracking numbers in the order screen, record which parcel arrived and avoid describing the whole order as delivered when one package remains outstanding.": "The official shipping page says available items may ship before pre-ordered or back-ordered products. If an order creates two parcels, each needs its own timeline. Match items to tracking numbers in the order screen, record which parcel arrived and avoid describing the whole order as delivered when one package remains outstanding.",
    "At delivery, photograph the label and contents if something is missing, damaged or incorrect. Keep the packaging while the issue is reviewed. A clean record connects the received parcel to the relevant line items and avoids confusing an unshipped product with a missing item from a delivered box. This distinction is especially important when support asks for evidence within a limited after-sales window.": "At delivery, photograph the label and contents if something is missing, damaged or incorrect. Keep the packaging while the issue is reviewed. A clean record connects the received parcel to the relevant line items and avoids confusing an unshipped product with a missing item from a delivered box. This distinction is especially important when support asks for evidence within a limited after-sales window.",
    "Build a support-ready tracking record": "Build a support-ready tracking record",
    "A useful record fits on one page: order identifier kept private, product or parcel concerned, order date, dispatch date, both tracking numbers if there was a handoff, last confirmed event, expected range and the action already taken with the carrier. Attach only relevant screenshots and remove unrelated personal information. State the resolution you need, such as a status investigation or the next official step.": "A useful record fits on one page: order identifier kept private, product or parcel concerned, order date, dispatch date, both tracking numbers if there was a handoff, last confirmed event, expected range and the action already taken with the carrier. Attach only relevant screenshots and remove unrelated personal information. State the resolution you need, such as a status investigation or the next official step.",
    "Independent guides can explain the sequence but cannot see an account or change a shipment. Use them to understand the evidence, then move the issue to the platform and carrier that control the order. Tracking becomes less confusing when every label is treated as a dated event with a limited meaning. That approach also gives support something concrete to investigate instead of a vague claim that the parcel disappeared.": "Independent guides can explain the sequence but cannot see an account or change a shipment. Use them to understand the evidence, then move the issue to the platform and carrier that control the order. Tracking becomes less confusing when every label is treated as a dated event with a limited meaning. That approach also gives support something concrete to investigate instead of a vague claim that the parcel disappeared.",
    "Protect yourself from tracking messages": "Protect yourself from tracking messages",
    "International deliveries often attract convincing text or email messages about a failed address, customs charge or redelivery. Do not use the message link first. Open the official app, retrieve the tracking number and visit the carrier through a saved bookmark or independently typed domain. Compare the claimed event with the carrier record before entering personal or payment information.": "International deliveries often attract convincing text or email messages about a failed address, customs charge or redelivery. Do not use the message link first. Open the official app, retrieve the tracking number and visit the carrier through a saved bookmark or independently typed domain. Compare the claimed event with the carrier record before entering personal or payment information.",
    "A legitimate parcel can still be used as the subject of a fraudulent message. The presence of a real tracking number is not enough to trust the sender. Save suspicious messages if support or the carrier needs them, then report through the relevant official channel. Security checks belong in the tracking workflow because a rushed response can cause more harm than a short delay.": "A legitimate parcel can still be used as the subject of a fraudulent message. The presence of a real tracking number is not enough to trust the sender. Save suspicious messages if support or the carrier needs them, then report through the relevant official channel. Security checks belong in the tracking workflow because a rushed response can cause more harm than a short delay.",
    "Close the timeline after delivery": "Close the timeline after delivery",
    "Once the parcel arrives, save the final delivery event and compare the contents with the parcel assignment. Inspect material problems promptly while the published after-sales period remains open. A delivery scan ends the transport timeline, but it does not resolve a missing item, wrong variant or damage claim. Those issues begin a separate evidence process.": "Once the parcel arrives, save the final delivery event and compare the contents with the parcel assignment. Inspect material problems promptly while the published after-sales period remains open. A delivery scan ends the transport timeline, but it does not resolve a missing item, wrong variant or damage claim. Those issues begin a separate evidence process.",
    "If everything is correct, remove sensitive screenshots from shared devices and retain only the records needed for warranty, return or payment purposes. A complete closed timeline helps you evaluate future estimates without treating one experience as universal. Use it as a dated example of one route, not as a promise of how the next Hacoo order will move.": "If everything is correct, remove sensitive screenshots from shared devices and retain only the records needed for warranty, return or payment purposes. A complete closed timeline helps you evaluate future estimates without treating one experience as universal. Use it as a dated example of one route, not as a promise of how the next Hacoo order will move.",
